<title>UK: UK, Irish green rates to revalue Saturday - HGCA.</title>
<headline>UK, Irish green rates to revalue Saturday - HGCA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green sterling and Irish pound rates will be revalued with effect from Saturday, the UK's Home Grown Cereals Authority said.</p>
<p>The new rates will be 0.742320 per ECU for sterling, compared with the old rate of 0.768177 and 0.756658 for the Irish pound, compared to the old rate of 0.778173.</p>
<p>The change comes at the end of five confirmation periods during which the two currencies have sustained high values against other EU currencies.</p>
<p>The change was calculated using rates up to Thursday because of the holiday on Friday.</p>
<p>Green rates are used by the European Union to convert amounts set in ECU under its Common Agricultural Policy into national currencies.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
</text>
